  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145492",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 243,
      "videoOrder": 227,
      "sourceHash": "28bb6b81b027f46b9ce166119b8b3da0a93e529f4efb6b3a668041ea0dea9e4f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.285,
          "end": 3.118,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] And that is it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.118,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "for this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 9.15,
          "en": "We've now had a detailed look at file based routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.15,
          "end": 13.3,
          "en": "and how we set up pages and how we navigate between pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.3,
          "end": 15.87,
          "en": "with Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 20.24,
          "en": "We had a look at the pages directory and that the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.24,
          "end": 22.79,
          "en": "and folders in there have a special meaning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.79,
          "end": 26.56,
          "en": "Index JS is always treated as a route page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.56,
          "end": 28.19,
          "en": "for the given folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.19,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "So either the overall route page, if it's an index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 36.38,
          "en": "JS file in pages or in portfolio or other sub folders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 41.78,
          "en": "Index JS would be loaded for /portfolio/ nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.16,
          "end": 45.73,
          "en": "We also can have other file names to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.73,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "load/portfolio/list, and then load this list page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 54.39,
          "en": "And we can also have dynamic segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.39,
          "end": 59.39,
          "en": "by enclosing placeholder identifiers in square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.8,
          "end": 62.36,
          "en": "and then loading different kinds of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.36,
          "end": 66.07,
          "en": "for different concrete values we might be getting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.07,
          "end": 68.93,
          "en": "And we get access to the concrete value entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.93,
          "end": 73.01,
          "en": "for a POV segment, through the use router hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.01,
          "end": 73.873,
          "en": "as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.88,
          "end": 77.97,
          "en": "Now, we can also have nested dynamic segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.97,
          "end": 80.27,
          "en": "as we did with clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.27,
          "end": 85.13,
          "en": "And we can also have such catch-all files here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.13,
          "end": 88,
          "en": "by having square brackets and then three dots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88,
          "end": 91.37,
          "en": "in front of any identifier of our choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.37,
          "end": 94.94,
          "en": "And that allows us to catch multiple dynamic segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.94,
          "end": 96.44,
          "en": "in one go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.44,
          "end": 98.99000000000001,
          "en": "And all these are very powerful features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.99000000000001,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "for loading pages in exactly the way you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 105.14,
          "en": "Now for navigating around we want to use the link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.14,
          "end": 108.03999999999999,
          "en": "component provided by Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.03999999999999,
          "end": 110.72999999999999,
          "en": "or, if we need to navigate programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.72999999999999,
          "end": 113.22999999999999,
          "en": "we can do that through that router object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.22999999999999,
          "end": 117.66,
          "en": "which we get through use router or in class-based components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.66,
          "end": 120.823,
          "en": "through to with router, higher order component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.81,
          "end": 125.05,
          "en": "And therefore, we now know what file-based routing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.05,
          "end": 126.41,
          "en": "and how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.41,
          "end": 129.88,
          "en": "But is that now better than the code-based approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.88,
          "end": 132.99,
          "en": "we know from standard react projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.99,
          "end": 136,
          "en": "that do not use Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136,
          "end": 138.82999999999998,
          "en": "Ultimately that is, of course, up to you to decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.82999999999998,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "but I want to give you my perspective on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.123,
          "en": "and a small comparison I came up with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.12,
          "end": 148.05,
          "en": "When we compare file-based routing, which we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.05,
          "end": 151.44,
          "en": "with Next.js to this standard code-based routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.44,
          "end": 154.91,
          "en": "we have in standard react apps with react router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.91,
          "end": 157.91,
          "en": "then in the case of file-based routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.91,
          "end": 162.42000000000002,
          "en": "we have no extra boiler plate code that needs to be written.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.42000000000002,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "So this kind of route configuration, which we need to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 170.03,
          "en": "in our react components when using react router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.03,
          "end": 173.22,
          "en": "that is not required with Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.22,
          "end": 175.89,
          "en": "and the file-based routing system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.89,
          "end": 179.42000000000002,
          "en": "Instead of writing this boiler plate code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.42000000000002,
          "end": 181.98,
          "en": "we simply create component files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.98,
          "end": 184.23,
          "en": "which we would need to do anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.23,
          "end": 189.01,
          "en": "and we just store them in a structure that replicates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.01,
          "end": 192.8,
          "en": "the path we want to have in our URL in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.8,
          "end": 197.09,
          "en": "And that in my opinion is a very natural way of, well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.09,
          "end": 199.29,
          "en": "setting up all our page components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.29,
          "end": 201.88,
          "en": "and of storing our page components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.88,
          "end": 205.01,
          "en": "So therefore, we do something we need to do anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.01,
          "end": 208.73,
          "en": "and we save the other part of creating extra code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.73,
          "end": 211.9,
          "en": "just to tell react which components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.9,
          "end": 214.19,
          "en": "should be loaded for which path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.19,
          "end": 217.63,
          "en": "We combined that into one step instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.63,
          "end": 221.32,
          "en": "Therefore, in my opinion, that's a very intuitive system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.32,
          "end": 224.89,
          "en": "of creating components and of storing components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.89,
          "end": 226.75,
          "en": "and of setting up routing, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.75,
          "end": 228.75,
          "en": "We don't need to do anything for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.75,
          "end": 231.51,
          "en": "We get the routing for free, if you want to call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.51,
          "end": 232.73,
          "en": "like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.73,
          "end": 236.09,
          "en": "So with file-based routing the file and folder structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.09,
          "end": 239.72,
          "en": "we have is everything that influences our routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.72,
          "end": 243.24,
          "en": "And we, therefore, fully control the POVs we support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.24,
          "end": 246.61,
          "en": "in our application, through our folder structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.61,
          "end": 248.9,
          "en": "in that pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.9,
          "end": 251.68,
          "en": "Now for navigating around, we use a link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.68,
          "end": 254.22,
          "en": "and we can also navigate imperatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 256.303,
          "en": "so there's nothing special about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.2,
          "end": 259.67,
          "en": "Now for a code-based routing, we do have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.67,
          "end": 262.72,
          "en": "that extra boiler plate set up in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.72,
          "end": 265.76,
          "en": "Though, of course, you could argue that by doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.76,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "you have some code where you can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 270.34,
          "en": "which routes are supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.34,
          "end": 272.94,
          "en": "You don't need to look at the file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.94,
          "end": 275.29,
          "en": "though I would argue that looking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.29,
          "end": 278.22,
          "en": "at the file system wouldn't be too difficult,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.22,
          "end": 280.08,
          "en": "but of course, ultimately that's of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.08,
          "end": 281.90999999999997,
          "en": "up to you to judge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.90999999999997,
          "end": 284.05,
          "en": "Now, it is definitely straightforward,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.05,
          "end": 287.21,
          "en": "don't get me wrong, but it includes new components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 287.21,
          "end": 288.89,
          "en": "and concepts, which you need to learn,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.89,
          "end": 291.56,
          "en": "like that switch component, and that route component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.56,
          "end": 294.21,
          "en": "and how to order your routes and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.21,
          "end": 296.6,
          "en": "So that can be annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 296.6,
          "end": 298.61,
          "en": "Now a potential advantage, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 298.61,
          "end": 300.52,
          "en": "is that the file and folders set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 300.52,
          "end": 302.27,
          "en": "does not matter at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.27,
          "end": 305.042,
          "en": "In my opinion, having the folder structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 305.042,
          "end": 308.38,
          "en": "dictate the POS is an advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.38,
          "end": 311.17,
          "en": "but you could see this as a disadvantage as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 311.17,
          "end": 314.21,
          "en": "And with code-based routing you can store your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.21,
          "end": 315.63,
          "en": "files wherever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 315.63,
          "end": 320.19,
          "en": "They won't have any influence on your routes or your POS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.19,
          "end": 323.94,
          "en": "Now navigation works pretty much as it does with Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 323.94,
          "end": 325.41,
          "en": "You have a link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 327.85,
          "en": "and you can also navigate imperatively there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327.85,
          "end": 330.03,
          "en": "So no differences there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 330.03,
          "end": 331.89,
          "en": "Therefore, overall, in my opinion,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 331.89,
          "end": 334.17,
          "en": "file-based routing is more intuitive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.17,
          "end": 336.79,
          "en": "and is easier to set up, but it is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.79,
          "end": 338.3,
          "en": "up to you to judge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.3,
          "end": 343.3,
          "en": "Either way, it is how Next.js thinks about pages and routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.7,
          "end": 346.33,
          "en": "And therefore, when working with Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.33,
          "end": 349.203,
          "en": "you want to embrace that file-based approach.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
